<section class="about" id="about">
  <div class="about__inner">
    <span class="eyebrow about__eyebrow">About</span>

    <p class="about__lede">
      I'm a software engineer<br>
      <em class="serif-italic">building for communities.</em><br>
      Understand how people work,<br>
      Discern their real needs,<br>
      And ship what fits.
    </p>

    <p class="about__body">
      Seven years professionally on AWS: cloud-native infrastructure, event-driven
      systems, full-stack applications. Most recently at United Airlines, where I drove
      on-prem to cloud system migrations and led a cross-team effort that resolved
      16,000+ CVEs in a year. Startups and enterprises both, multiple stacks.
    </p>

    <p class="about__body">
      I apply the same instinct to human systems. The Melty Blood community was rough on
      newcomers and rough on itself, so I designed a weekly event series with formats,
      scheduling, and rules engineered to nudge the scene toward a healthier culture. Offline
      major attendance went from under 100 to 200+ players, sustained since 2024. I built tools to
      streamline tournament organization for other organizers, and I mentor both engineers
      and competitors in the scenes I'm part of.
    </p>

    <p class="about__body">
      I'm building, learning, and <strong>open to freelance and full-time work</strong>.
      Platform, DevEx, and engineering enablement is where this synthesis lands sharpest,
      but the same instinct comes with whatever I'm hired to do. If you need someone to
      walk into your workflow, ship what's missing, and strengthen the team behind it,
      <a href="#contact">get in touch</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

